    "question": "At which temperature and voltage is the pinch stop time worst, according to our lessons learned?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "According to the lessons learned, pinch stop time is worst at -30 °C and 9 V, the cold and low-voltage corner case. In the WLC-100 winter testing, stop time there was 12 to 15 ms against a 10 ms limit, compared with 5 to 7 ms at 23 °C. The lessons learned state that the worst case is cold and low voltage together, so this corner should be tested on every software release.",
