    "id": "q05",
    "question": "How is the stop latency measured in the anti-pinch test?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "Stop latency is the time from the first log sample where the pinch force is above 80 N to the first later sample where the motor command is no longer 'close', with a limit of 10 ms. The bench guide says anti-pinch tests are logged at 1 ms (only thermal tests use 10 ms), so the measurement resolution is 1 ms.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "document": "TP-AP-01-anti-pinch-test.md",
          "text": "from the first sample where the pinch force is above 80 N to the first later sample where the motor command is no longer 'close'"
        },
        {
          "document": "GL-HIL-2-bench-guide.md",
          "text": "1 ms for all tests except the thermal tests, which use 10 ms"
        }
      ]
    },
