    "id": "q08",
    "question": "Why could a movement start above the thermal block limit on SMC-3?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "The thermal model updated its temperature estimate in a 100 ms task, but the block decision read that estimate at the start of a movement, before the task had run with the newest current samples, so one movement could start on a stale value. The documents describe this as the root cause in LL-2024-01 (seat motor controller SMC-3, a different product on the same software platform as WLC-200). The fix is that the block decision now reads the estimate after the thermal task has run in the same cycle. The documents don't say whether this fix is present in WLC-200, only that the platform thermal module is shared and should be checked.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-01-thermal-check.md",
          "text": "The thermal model updated its estimate in a 100 ms task. The block decision read the estimate at the start of a movement, before the task had run with the newest current samples."
        },
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-01-thermal-check.md",
          "text": "One movement could start on a stale value."
        }
      ]
    },
