    "id": "q09",
    "question": "What caused lost status frames in WLC-100 diagnostic sessions?",
    "answer": {
      "found": true,
      "answer": "During a diagnostic session, long diagnostic responses filled the CAN transmit queue, so a status frame due at that moment was dropped instead of delayed. This produced gaps of about 100 to 150 ms in the status frames the body controller logged, and it showed up only in the service workshop. The fix enlarged the transmit queue and gave status frames their own transmit buffer.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-09-can-frame-loss.md",
          "text": "During a diagnostic session, long diagnostic responses filled the CAN transmit queue. A status frame due at that moment was dropped instead of being delayed."
        },
        {
          "document": "LL-2024-09-can-frame-loss.md",
          "text": "The transmit queue was enlarged, and status frames got their own transmit buffer."
        }
      ]
    },
